+# [ARCHITECTURE_PLAN]
+
+## Topic
+
+Request/correlation id propagation — `docs/arch/request-id.md`
+
+A single HTTP header carrying a per-request correlation id, reused when a caller already supplies one and
+generated otherwise, always present on the response, and readable by application code while the request is
+being handled — identically whether the app runs on the Express or the Fastify platform integration.
+
+## Implementation Order
+
+1. **`packages/core/request-id`** (new) — has no `Imports` from any other documented cell, so it is designed
+   and implemented first. It depends only on Node's built-in `node:async_hooks` and `node:crypto`, and on the
+   `NestMiddleware` shape already established by `packages/common/interfaces/middleware` (not a documented
+   cell, referenced only in prose).
+
+No existing CODEMANIFEST needs modification: this feature does not change the contract of `core/adapters`,
+`core/router`, `platform-express/adapters`, or `platform-fastify/adapters` — it only relies on the existing,
+already-documented fact that `AbstractHttpAdapter` subclasses expose a uniform `use()` registration point, and
+that both concrete adapters ultimately hand registered middleware the platform's raw request/response objects.
+
+## Artifacts
+
+### Cell: `packages/core/request-id` (created)
+
+**CODEMANIFEST**
+
+```yaml
+Usages:
+  header_convention: |
+    The correlation id travels as a single HTTP header, read case-insensitively and always written back
+    using the canonical name `X-Request-Id`. Reuse an inbound value verbatim when present and non-empty;
+    only generate a new id when the header is absent or empty. Never emit more than one value for the
+    header on a given response.
+
+Annotations: |
+  Implements request/correlation id propagation for one incoming HTTP request, uniformly across every
+  platform HTTP adapter the framework bundles (Express, Fastify). Every request/response object this cell
+  touches is treated only as a plain Node.js `http.IncomingMessage`/`http.ServerResponse` surface (`headers`,
+  `setHeader`, `getHeader`) — never a platform-specific wrapper — because that is the shape both bundled
+  platform integrations hand to middleware registered through `HttpServer.use()` / `MiddlewareConsumer`.
+  Use `header_convention` for header handling.
+
+---
+
+"RequestIdStorage()":
+  location: request-id.storage.ts
+  annotations: |
+    Static holder that publishes the resolved id for the current request to any code running within it, via
+    Node's AsyncLocalStorage, so application code can read the same id `RequestIdMiddleware` writes to the
+    response header without receiving it as an explicit argument or parsing the response.
+
+    Algorithm:
+    1. Hold a single module-level `AsyncLocalStorage<string>` instance for the lifetime of the process.
+  methods:
+    "run(id: string, callback: Object<string, any>) -> result: any": |
+      Run `callback` with `id` bound as the active request id for the duration of its execution, including
+      further async continuations scheduled from within it.
+
+      `id`: the resolved request/correlation id to publish
+      `callback`: the function to execute with `id` active; its return value is passed through unchanged
+
+      Requirements:
+      - Code awaited or scheduled from within `callback` must still observe `id` via `getId()`.
+    "getId() -> id: string | null": |
+      Return the id active for the currently executing asynchronous context.
+
+      `id`: the active request id, or `null` when called outside of a `run` scope
+
+"RequestIdMiddleware()":
+  location: request-id.middleware.ts
+  annotations: |
+    Injectable, platform-agnostic middleware that resolves the request/correlation id for one incoming
+    request, exposes it to application code via `RequestIdStorage`, and guarantees it is present on the
+    outgoing response. Implements the framework's `NestMiddleware` shape (a `use(req, res, next)` method) so
+    it can be registered through `MiddlewareConsumer.apply(...).forRoutes(...)` the same way on every
+    platform integration.
+
+    Algorithm:
+    1. Read the inbound value of the `X-Request-Id` header from `req`, matched case-insensitively
+    2. When present and non-empty, reuse it verbatim as the request id; otherwise generate a new id
+    3. Write the resolved id back onto `res` under `X-Request-Id`, per `header_convention`
+    4. Invoke `next` via `RequestIdStorage.run`, so the resolved id is active for every downstream guard,
+       interceptor, pipe, handler, and exception filter for this request
+
+    Requirements:
+    - The id observed via `RequestIdStorage.getId()` anywhere during this request must equal the value sent
+      back in the `X-Request-Id` response header.
+  methods:
+    "use(req: any, res: any, next: Object<string, any>)": |
+      Resolve and publish the request id for one request-response cycle, per the type's Algorithm.
+
+---
+
+Author: Goga
+CreatedAt: 14/09/26
+Description: |
+  Documents request/correlation id propagation: resolving (or reusing) a per-request id, returning it on
+  every HTTP response, and publishing it to application code for the duration of the request, uniformly
+  across the Express and Fastify platform integrations.
+```
+
+**`.usages/` files** — none. `header_convention` is short (a few sentences, specific to this cell) and is kept
+inline per the cookbook's inline-form guidance rather than split into a file.
+
+## Dependency Map
+
+```
+packages/core/request-id   (no Imports — leaf cell)
+```
+
+No other cell imports from `packages/core/request-id` as part of this change; it is consumed at the
+application layer (via `MiddlewareConsumer` and direct calls to `RequestIdStorage.getId()`), not by other
+framework cells.
+
+## Verification Checklist
+
+- `RequestIdStorage.run`/`getId` round-trip an id correctly across at least one `await` boundary (proves
+  `AsyncLocalStorage` context survives async continuations).
+- `RequestIdMiddleware` reuses an inbound `X-Request-Id` header verbatim instead of generating a new one.
+- `RequestIdMiddleware` generates a new id (non-empty, unique per request) when no header is supplied.
+- The resolved id appears on the outgoing response's `X-Request-Id` header in both cases.
+- A value read via `RequestIdStorage.getId()` from inside a controller handler equals the response header
+  value, on both the default (Express) adapter and `FastifyAdapter`, using the same application code.
+- `goga lint` passes for the new cell.
